You are given $*N*$ qubits ($1 ≤ *N* ≤ 8$) in zero state ![image](https://espresso.codeforces.com/8bb67080da7081bfb802ca6ecc5abc4f4c5ca190.png). Your task is to create Greenberger–Horne–Zeilinger (GHZ) state on them:

![image](https://espresso.codeforces.com/acb08ce15c611d90dc85f731accccd9bbfac8fd3.png)

Note that for $*N* = 1$ and $*N* = 2$ GHZ state becomes states ![image](https://espresso.codeforces.com/891b1e75c93e44f237b7fde497062f8e85c1d952.png) and ![image](https://espresso.codeforces.com/aec27febc80bfeb882cb96d33386f048ce011703.png) from the previous tasks, respectively.

## Input

You have to implement an operation which takes an array of $*N*$ qubits as an input and has no output. The "output" of your solution is the state in which it left the input qubits.

Your code should have the following signature:

```
namespace Solution {
    open Microsoft.Quantum.Primitive;
    open Microsoft.Quantum.Canon;

    operation Solve (qs : Qubit[]) : ()
    {
        body
        {
            // your code here
        }
    }
}
```
